[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Start "ruy-modern 7.c3"]
[Name "...Bc5 and ...d6"]

7... d6 { Keeps e5 firm. Now e5 will not chase the f6 knight so easily. }
8. d4 { The same push, hitting the bishop. }
8... exd4 9. cxd4 Bb6
10. Nc3 { Develops and adds to the pressure on d5. With ...d6 played, there is no rush to push e5. [%cal Gc3d5] }
10... O-O
11. Bg5 { Pins the knight on f6 to the queen. Nd5 comes next, and White's pieces all point at f6. [%cal Gg5f6,Gc3d5] [%idea pin] } *
